            <div xml:id="d179-a2">

                <pb facs="0351" n="1005" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1005"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No 14.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Torre to Mr. Gibbs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-08-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 10, 1875</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg></opener>
                <p>I regret to inform your excellency that the prefect of Callao has just announced
                    to me Admiral Collins died yesterday at 9.45 p.m. In bringing this sad news to
                    your excellency’s knowledge, I take occasion to inform you that measures have
                    been taken by the minister of marine, in order that such honors as befit his
                    high rank may be paid to the departed admiral at the funeral, which is to take
                    place to-morrow, in pursuance of arrangements made by the American consulate at
                    Callao. I avail myself of this sad occasion to reiterate to your excellency the
                    assurances of my distinguished consideration and esteem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. V. de la</hi>
                    TORRE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Gibbs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Plenipotentiary of the United States of
                            North America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
